{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "def common_in_nested_lists(list_of_lists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds common integers across all nested lists.\n    Raises TypeError for invalid input types or non-integer elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validate input type\n    if not isinstance(list_of_lists, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list of lists of integers.\")\n\n    # Handle empty input\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        return set()\n\n    # Convert each sub-list to a set to remove duplicates\n    try:\n        sets = [set(sublist) for sublist in list_of_lists]\n    except TypeError:\n        raise TypeError(\"All elements must be integers.\")\n\n    # Compute intersection\n    common = set.intersection(*sets)\n    return common"}
