{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "memo = {}\ndef get_max_sum(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum possible by using the given equation\n    f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\n    Uses memoization to avoid redundant calculations.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return 0\n\n    if n in memo:\n        return memo[n]\n\n    sum_parts = (get_max_sum(n // 2) +\n                 get_max_sum(n // 3) +\n                 get_max_sum(n // 4) +\n                 get_max_sum(n // 5))\n\n    result = max(sum_parts, n)\n    memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
