{"task_id": "Mbpp/440", "solution": "import re\nfrom typing import Optional, Tuple\ndef find_adverb_position(sentence: str) -> Tuple[Optional[int], Optional[int], Optional[str]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first adverb and its position in a given sentence.\n    It first attempts to use NLTK for POS tagging, falling back to a regex pattern if NLTK fails.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _detect_with_nltk_inline(text: str) -> Optional[Tuple[int, int, str]]:\n        \"\"\"Attempts to find the first adverb using NLTK POS tagging.\"\"\"\n        import nltk\n        tokens = nltk.word_tokenize(text)\n        tags = nltk.pos_tag(tokens)\n        \n        for token, tag in tags:\n            if tag in ('RB', 'RBR', 'RBS'): # Adverb, Comparative Adverb, Superlative Adverb\n                start_pos = text.find(token)\n                if start_pos != -1: # Ensure the token exists in the original string\n                    return (start_pos, start_pos + len(token), token)\n        return None\n\n    def _detect_with_regex_inline(text: str) -> Optional[Tuple[int, int, str]]:\n        \"\"\"Finds the first word ending in -ly using regex.\"\"\"\n        pattern = re.compile(r'\\b(\\w+ly)\\b', re.IGNORECASE)\n        match = pattern.search(text)\n        if match:\n            word = match.group(1)\n            start_pos = match.start(1)\n            end_pos = match.end(1)\n            return (start_pos, end_pos, word)\n        return None\n\n    adverb_info: Optional[Tuple[int, int, str]] = None\n    try:\n        adverb_info = _detect_with_nltk_inline(sentence)\n    except Exception: # Catches errors like ModuleNotFoundError if NLTK is not installed/configured\n        adverb_info = _detect_with_regex_inline(sentence)\n    \n    if adverb_info:\n        return adverb_info\n    \n    return (None, None, None)"}
