{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple, Set\ndef tuple_intersection(list1: List[Tuple[int, int]], list2: List[Tuple[int, int]]) -> Set[Tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the intersection of two lists of tuples, treating tuples with the same elements\n    but different order as identical.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _normalize_tuple(t: Tuple[int, int]) -> Tuple[int, int]:\n        \"\"\"Returns a tuple with its elements sorted to create a canonical representation.\"\"\"\n        return tuple(sorted(t))\n\n    normalized_set1 = {_normalize_tuple(t) for t in list1}\n    normalized_set2 = {_normalize_tuple(t) for t in list2}\n\n    return normalized_set1.intersection(normalized_set2)"}
