{"task_id": "Mbpp/765", "solution": "import math\ndef is_polite(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the nth polite number.\n    A polite number is a positive integer that is not a power of two.\n    \"\"\"\n    # The nth polite number 'x' satisfies x - (floor(log2(x)) + 1) = n.\n    # This implies x = n + floor(log2(x)) + 1. We iterate to find x.\n    \n    x = n\n    while True:\n        # Calculate count of powers of two up to current x.\n        # For x >= 1, this is int(log2(x)) + 1.\n        powers_of_two_count = int(math.log2(x)) + 1\n        \n        # Determine the next candidate for x based on the formula.\n        next_x = n + powers_of_two_count\n        \n        # If x has converged, return it.\n        if next_x == x:\n            return x\n        \n        x = next_x"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/767", "solution": "def get_pairs_count(numbers: list[int], sum: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of unordered pairs in the list whose sum is equal to the target sum.\n    Each element's position contributes to distinct pairs, even if values are identical.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    n = len(numbers)\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if numbers[i] + numbers[j] == sum:\n                count += 1\n    return count"}
