{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef right_insertion(elements: List[int], value: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the right insertion point for a specified value in a sorted list.\n    This function finds the index where 'value' can be inserted to maintain sorted order,\n    ensuring it's placed after any existing elements equal to 'value'.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(elements)\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if elements[mid] <= value:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    return low"}
