{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "def sum_in_range(l: int, r: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the sum of all odd natural numbers within the inclusive range [l, r].\n    Returns 0 if l == r or l > r.\n    \"\"\"\n    if l >= r:  # Handles l > r and l == r\n        return 0\n\n    total = 0\n    # Ensure starting at the first odd number within the range\n    start = l if l % 2 == 1 else l + 1\n    \n    # Iterate from start to r (inclusive), stepping by 2 to get only odd numbers\n    for num in range(start, r + 1, 2):\n        total += num\n        \n    return total"}
