{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number, d):\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates the bits of a 32-bit number to the left by `d` positions, wrapping around.\n    The number is assumed to be an unsigned 32-bit integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    INT_BITS = 32\n    MAX_32BIT = (1 << INT_BITS) - 1\n\n    # Normalize the rotation amount to be within 0 to INT_BITS-1.\n    d_effective = d % INT_BITS\n\n    # Perform the left rotation: (bits shifted left) | (bits wrapped around from MSB to LSB).\n    # The final result is masked to ensure it remains a 32-bit number.\n    return ((number << d_effective) | (number >> (INT_BITS - d_effective))) & MAX_32BIT"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/801", "solution": "def test_three_equal(a, b, c):\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of equal integers among three given numbers.\"\"\"\n    if a == b and b == c:\n        return 3\n    elif a == b or b == c or a == c:\n        return 2\n    else:\n        return 0"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/803", "solution": "def is_perfect_square(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number is a perfect square using only integer arithmetic.\n    It employs a binary search approach to find the integer square root.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return False\n    if number == 0:\n        return True\n\n    low = 1\n    high = number  # The square root of 'number' cannot exceed 'number' itself.\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        mid_squared = mid * mid\n\n        if mid_squared == number:\n            return True\n        elif mid_squared < number:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n\n    return False"}
