{"task_id": "Mbpp/12", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef _compute_row_sums(matrix: List[List[int]]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Computes the sum of each row in the matrix.\"\"\"\n    return [sum(row) for row in matrix]\ndef _stable_sort_rows(rows: List[List[int]], sums: List[int]) -> List[List[int]]:\n    \"\"\"Performs a stable sort on rows based on their corresponding sums.\"\"\"\n    # Pair rows with their sums and sort them based on the sum\n    paired_rows_with_sums = list(zip(rows, sums))\n    sorted_pairs = sorted(paired_rows_with_sums, key=lambda item: item[1])\n    # Extract the sorted rows from the pairs\n    return [row for row, _sum in sorted_pairs]\ndef sort_matrix(matrix: List[List[int]]) -> List[List[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a given matrix in ascending order according to the sum of its rows.\n    Returns a new matrix, preserving the original.\n    \"\"\"\n    row_sums = _compute_row_sums(matrix)\n    sorted_rows = _stable_sort_rows(matrix, row_sums)\n    # Create a new matrix by shallow copying each row to ensure the returned structure is new.\n    return [row[:] for row in sorted_rows]"}
