{"task_id": "Mbpp/14", "solution": "class TriangularPrism:\n    def __init__(self, base: float, height: float, length: float):\n        if base <= 0 or height <= 0 or length <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Base, height, and length must be positive.\")\n        self.base = base\n        self.height = height\n        self.length = length\n\n    def computeVolume(self) -> float:\n        return 0.5 * self.base * self.height * self.length\ndef find_Volume(base: float, height: float, length: float) -> float:\n    prism = TriangularPrism(base, height, length)\n    return prism.computeVolume()"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/9", "solution": "def find_Rotations(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum positive number of rotations to restore the original string.\n    Returns 1 for strings with all identical characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n\n    # Handles strings like \"aaaa\" and also the single character string \"a\".\n    if s.count(s[0]) == n:\n        return 1\n\n    double_s = s + s\n    for k in range(1, n + 1):\n        if double_s[k:k + n] == s:\n            return k"}
