{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence using dynamic programming.\n    The sequence starts with a(1)=1, a(2)=1, and a(n) = a(a(n-1)) + a(n-a(n-1)) for n > 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1 or n == 2:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize a list to store sequence terms, 1-indexed.\n    # dp[0] is unused; dp[i] stores the ith term of the sequence.\n    dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n    dp[1] = 1\n    dp[2] = 1\n\n    # Compute terms from the 3rd up to the nth term using the recurrence relation.\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        dp[i] = dp[dp[i - 1]] + dp[i - dp[i - 1]]\n\n    return dp[n]"}
