{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, rotation_count: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the number of times a rotated binary string represents an odd integer.\n    Performs right-shift rotations and counts how many results are odd.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(binary_string)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    odd_count = 0\n    # Optimize by considering only rotations up to the string's length\n    effective_rotations = min(rotation_count, n) \n\n    # We need to compute string slicing for each rotation to simulate the shift.\n    # The initial string can be considered as the 0th rotation.\n    for _ in range(effective_rotations):\n        # Convert the current binary string to an integer and check if it's odd\n        # A binary number is odd if its last digit is '1'.\n        if binary_string[-1] == '1':\n            odd_count += 1\n        \n        # Perform a right-shift rotation\n        binary_string = binary_string[-1] + binary_string[:-1]\n\n    return odd_count"}
