{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "def sum_common_divisors(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of common divisors of two integers.\n    Uses GCD and then enumerates divisors of the GCD.\n    \"\"\"\n    if a == 0 or b == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Calculate GCD using the Euclidean algorithm\n    # Use absolute values to handle potential negative inputs gracefully\n    num1, num2 = abs(a), abs(b)\n    while num2:\n        num1, num2 = num2, num1 % num2\n    \n    gcd_val = num1\n    common_divisor_sum = 0\n    \n    # Find divisors of the GCD and sum them\n    # Iterate up to the square root of gcd_val for efficiency\n    i = 1\n    while i * i <= gcd_val:\n        if gcd_val % i == 0:\n            common_divisor_sum += i\n            if i * i != gcd_val:  # Add the pair divisor if it's distinct\n                common_divisor_sum += gcd_val // i\n        i += 1\n        \n    return common_divisor_sum"}
