{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(arr: list[int], n: int, element: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if an element is the majority element in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Find the first occurrence of the element using binary search.\n    left, right = 0, n - 1\n    first = -1\n    while left <= right:\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == element:\n            first = mid\n            right = mid - 1  # Try to find an earlier occurrence\n        elif arr[mid] < element:\n            left = mid + 1\n        else:  # arr[mid] > element\n            right = mid - 1\n\n    if first == -1:\n        return False  # Element not present in the array\n\n    # Find the last occurrence of the element using binary search, starting from 'first'.\n    left, right = first, n - 1\n    last = first # Initialize last to first, as we know element is at least at 'first'\n    while left <= right:\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == element:\n            last = mid\n            left = mid + 1  # Try to find a later occurrence\n        elif arr[mid] < element:\n            left = mid + 1\n        else:  # arr[mid] > element\n            right = mid - 1\n\n    count = last - first + 1\n    return count > n // 2"}
