{"task_id": "Mbpp/252", "solution": "import math\nfrom typing import Tuple, Union\ndef convert(number: Union[int, float, complex]) -> Tuple[float, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a complex number (or real number treated as complex) to polar coordinates.\n    Returns a tuple containing the magnitude and angle (in radians).\n    \"\"\"\n    real_part = float(number.real) if hasattr(number, 'real') else float(number)\n    imag_part = float(number.imag) if hasattr(number, 'imag') else 0.0\n\n    magnitude = math.sqrt(real_part**2 + imag_part**2)\n    angle = math.atan2(imag_part, real_part)\n\n    return magnitude, angle"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "def count_Primes_nums(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of prime numbers less than a given non-negative integer using the Sieve of Eratosthenes.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 2:\n        return 0\n\n    is_prime = [True] * n\n    is_prime[0] = is_prime[1] = False\n\n    for p in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if is_prime[p]:\n            for multiple in range(p * p, n, p):\n                is_prime[multiple] = False\n\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        if is_prime[i]:\n            count += 1\n    return count"}
