{"task_id": "Mbpp/259", "solution": "from typing import Tuple\ndef maximize_elements(\n    tuple_of_tuples1: Tuple[Tuple[int, ...], ...],\n    tuple_of_tuples2: Tuple[Tuple[int, ...], ...]\n) -> Tuple[Tuple[int, ...], ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a new tuple of tuples containing the element-wise maximum of the\n    corresponding inner tuples from the two input tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_list = []\n    for inner_tuple1, inner_tuple2 in zip(tuple_of_tuples1, tuple_of_tuples2):\n        maximized_inner_tuple = tuple(max(a, b) for a, b in zip(inner_tuple1, inner_tuple2))\n        result_list.append(maximized_inner_tuple)\n    return tuple(result_list)"}
