{"task_id": "Mbpp/261", "solution": "def division_elements(tuple1, tuple2):\n    \"\"\"Performs element-wise integer division of two tuples of equal length.\n    Raises ValueError for length mismatch or ZeroDivisionError for division by zero.\"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Tuples must be of the same length.\")\n\n    if 0 in tuple2:\n        raise ZeroDivisionError(\"Cannot divide by zero.\")\n\n    result = [n1 // n2 for n1, n2 in zip(tuple1, tuple2)]\n    return tuple(result)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/267", "solution": "def square_Sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the squares of the first n odd natural numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a non-negative integer\")\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        odd_number = 2 * i + 1\n        total_sum += odd_number * odd_number\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "from typing import List, Any\ndef list_split(lst: List[Any], n: int) -> List[List[Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits a list into n sublists, distributing elements cyclically.\n    Elements are appended to sublists based on their original index modulo n.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not lst:\n        return []\n\n    result: List[List[Any]] = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    for index, element in enumerate(lst):\n        sublist_index = index % n\n        result[sublist_index].append(element)\n\n    return result"}
