{"task_id": "Mbpp/445", "solution": "from typing import Tuple\ndef index_multiplication(\n    tuple1: Tuple[Tuple[int], ...],\n    tuple2: Tuple[Tuple[int], ...]\n) -> Tuple[Tuple[int], ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Perform element-wise multiplication of two tuples of tuples.\n    Raises ValueError if outer or inner lengths differ between inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not tuple1 and not tuple2:\n        return ()\n\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\n            \"Input tuples must have the same outer and inner lengths.\"\n        )\n\n    result = []\n    for idx, (inner1, inner2) in enumerate(zip(tuple1, tuple2)):\n        if len(inner1) != len(inner2):\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"Inner tuples at index {idx} have mismatched lengths.\"\n            )\n        product = tuple(a * b for a, b in zip(inner1, inner2))\n        result.append(product)\n\n    return tuple(result)"}
