{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "def cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers up to index n using an iterative O(n) time, O(1) space algorithm.\"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input n must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 3  # P(0) = 3\n    if n == 1:\n        return 3  # P(0) + P(1) = 3 + 0 = 3\n    if n == 2:\n        return 5  # P(0) + P(1) + P(2) = 3 + 0 + 2 = 5\n\n    # Initialize the first three Perrin numbers: P(0), P(1), P(2)\n    p_n_minus_3 = 3  # Corresponds to P(i-3)\n    p_n_minus_2 = 0  # Corresponds to P(i-2)\n    p_n_minus_1 = 2  # Corresponds to P(i-1)\n\n    # Initialize sum with P(0) + P(1) + P(2)\n    total_sum = 5\n\n    # Iterate from i = 3 up to n to calculate subsequent Perrin numbers and sum them\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        p_current = p_n_minus_3 + p_n_minus_2\n        total_sum += p_current\n\n        # Update the values for the next iteration\n        p_n_minus_3 = p_n_minus_2\n        p_n_minus_2 = p_n_minus_1\n        p_n_minus_1 = p_current\n\n    return total_sum"}
