{"task_id": "Mbpp/589", "solution": "import math\ndef perfect_squares(lower, upper):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds all perfect squares within the inclusive range [lower, upper].\n    \"\"\"\n    perfect_squares_list = []\n    # Calculate the smallest integer whose square is >= lower\n    start_num = math.ceil(math.sqrt(lower))\n    # Calculate the largest integer whose square is <= upper\n    end_num = math.floor(math.sqrt(upper))\n\n    for i in range(int(start_num), int(end_num) + 1):\n        square = i * i\n        if lower <= square <= upper: # Redundant check but ensures correctness for edge cases\n            perfect_squares_list.append(square)\n    return perfect_squares_list"}
