{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def get_median(list1: list[int], list2: list[int], n: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Finds the median of two sorted lists of the same size n.\"\"\"\n    i = 0\n    j = 0\n    merged_list = []\n\n    # Merge the two lists into a single sorted list\n    while i < n and j < n:\n        if list1[i] < list2[j]:\n            merged_list.append(list1[i])\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            merged_list.append(list2[j])\n            j += 1\n    \n    # Append any remaining elements from list1\n    while i < n:\n        merged_list.append(list1[i])\n        i += 1\n        \n    # Append any remaining elements from list2\n    while j < n:\n        merged_list.append(list2[j])\n        j += 1\n\n    # For an even-length combined list (2*n), the median is the average of the two middle elements.\n    median = (merged_list[n - 1] + merged_list[n]) / 2.0\n    \n    return median"}
